WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.030
Miranda is the smallest and innermost of Uranus's five round satellites.

00:05.487 --> 00:16.679
It was discovered by Gerard Kuiper on 16 February 1948 at McDonald Observatory in Texas, and named after Miranda from William Shakespeare's play The Tempest.

00:17.206 --> 00:22.841
Like the other large moons of Uranus, Miranda orbits close to its planet's equatorial plane.

00:23.431 --> 00:32.946
Because Uranus orbits the Sun on its side, Miranda's orbit is nearly perpendicular to the ecliptic and shares Uranus's extreme seasonal cycle.
